WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.498
Welcome to ADVISIO.

2
00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.934
This walkthrough follows the Defense
Panelist workspace:

3
00:00:05.364 --> 00:00:08.707
responding to invitations, preparing
manuscripts, recording

4
00:00:08.754 --> 00:00:12.399
assessments, and reviewing the
academic records available to you.

5
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.276
Sign in with your authorized panelist
account.

6
00:00:15.705 --> 00:00:19.014
Check the Defense Panelist workspace
and Panelist Center badge.

7
00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:23.124
This recording uses fictional groups
in an isolated local workspace,

8
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:26.328
with normal authentication and
assignment permissions.

9
00:00:26.933 --> 00:00:29.661
The Overview dashboard provides a
summary of your defense

10
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.844
assignments and evaluation activities.

11
00:00:32.274 --> 00:00:36.058
From here, you can check upcoming
sessions, access manuscripts for

12
00:00:36.116 --> 00:00:40.029
review, complete evaluations, and
revisit previously submitted

13
00:00:40.075 --> 00:00:40.609
records.

14
00:00:41.294 --> 00:00:44.220
The sidebar organizes these tools so
you can move between

15
00:00:44.278 --> 00:00:46.890
preparation, evaluation, and results.

16
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:50.791
Check the displayed assignment and
evaluation counts before choosing

17
00:00:50.838 --> 00:00:51.743
the next task.

18
00:00:52.428 --> 00:00:55.029
The demonstration records and accounts
are fictional.

19
00:00:55.633 --> 00:00:59.070
Defense Schedule displays your
assigned sessions and invitations.

20
00:00:59.662 --> 00:01:03.644
Before responding, review the research
project, proposed date and

21
00:01:03.714 --> 00:01:06.941
time, session arrangements, and your
assigned role.

22
00:01:07.626 --> 00:01:10.853
Opening the defense details provides
additional information to help

23
00:01:10.911 --> 00:01:12.304
you prepare for the assignment.

24
00:01:12.804 --> 00:01:16.147
The invitation remains pending until
you submit your response.

25
00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:19.456
Opening the details does not accept
the assignment.

26
00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.970
If you're available to serve as a
panelist, select Accept

27
00:01:23.017 --> 00:01:23.737
Invitation.

28
00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.035
Your response is recorded in the
system.

29
00:01:26.535 --> 00:01:30.424
If you cannot attend, choose Decline
and provide any requested

30
00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:33.663
information so the coordinator can
make the necessary arrangements.

31
00:01:34.162 --> 00:01:37.285
For this walkthrough, we'll continue
with an accepted assignment.

32
00:01:37.715 --> 00:01:41.592
Acceptance and decline use separate
demonstration sessions, so the

33
00:01:41.627 --> 00:01:44.924
accepted assignment remains available
for the preparation scenes.

34
00:01:45.533 --> 00:01:49.144
After accepting the invitation, you
can access the defense workspace

35
00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.036
and its available session information.

36
00:01:51.628 --> 00:01:54.995
This includes the scheduled defense,
participant details, and

37
00:01:55.053 --> 00:01:56.365
preparation materials.

38
00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.021
For online or hybrid defenses, the
workspace may also provide the

39
00:02:01.091 --> 00:02:02.948
meeting link needed to join the
session.

40
00:02:03.448 --> 00:02:06.431
A published packet and an accepted
invitation are separate

41
00:02:06.455 --> 00:02:07.151
conditions.

42
00:02:07.581 --> 00:02:10.797
Scoring still requires the coordinator
to start the defense.

43
00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.744
Once the defense packet is published,
accepted panelists can review

44
00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:15.974
the assigned manuscript.

45
00:02:16.566 --> 00:02:19.748
Open the manuscript to read the
document and examine the research

46
00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.327
before the scheduled defense.

47
00:02:21.919 --> 00:02:25.297
The workspace also keeps track of
document versions, helping you

48
00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.455
identify which manuscript is currently
assigned for review.

49
00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.544
Confirm the version labelled Published
for defense.

50
00:02:32.136 --> 00:02:34.493
Earlier review versions retain their
own history;

51
00:02:34.922 --> 00:02:38.254
do not assume an earlier annotation
belongs to a newly published

52
00:02:38.289 --> 00:02:39.125
manuscript.

53
00:02:39.733 --> 00:02:43.657
ADVISIO also provides annotation tools
for reviewing manuscripts.

54
00:02:44.087 --> 00:02:47.872
You can highlight important passages,
add comments, and mark areas

55
00:02:47.906 --> 00:02:50.345
that may require clarification or
revision.

56
00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:53.607
Your annotations are saved privately
while you work.

57
00:02:54.037 --> 00:02:57.079
When you're ready to share your
feedback, preview the annotated

58
00:02:57.137 --> 00:02:59.076
manuscript and review the changes.

59
00:02:59.505 --> 00:03:02.535
Selecting Share Feedback publishes a
copy for the authorized

60
00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.579
coordinator and research group
members.

61
00:03:05.008 --> 00:03:08.677
Your original manuscript remains
unchanged, and the shared feedback

62
00:03:08.747 --> 00:03:10.465
is preserved as a separate record.

63
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.563
Sharing feedback does not submit a
defense evaluation or select the

64
00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:15.771
official outcome.

65
00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:19.548
Once the coordinator starts the live
defense, the evaluation

66
00:03:19.618 --> 00:03:21.731
workspace becomes available for
scoring.

67
00:03:22.323 --> 00:03:25.667
Open the evaluation for the assigned
research group and confirm that

68
00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:28.639
you're using the correct form before
beginning your assessment.

69
00:03:29.068 --> 00:03:31.216
This is a separate prepared live
session.

70
00:03:31.715 --> 00:03:35.291
The panelist cannot start the
coordinator-managed defense or change

71
00:03:35.326 --> 00:03:37.265
its configured evaluation method.

72
00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:41.559
Some defenses use an existing PDF
evaluation form instead of a

73
00:03:41.605 --> 00:03:42.941
structured digital form.

74
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:46.992
In this workspace, you can complete
the document using checkmarks,

75
00:03:47.109 --> 00:03:49.965
circles, text, highlights, and
comments.

76
00:03:50.557 --> 00:03:53.042
You can also adjust your entries
before submitting.

77
00:03:53.471 --> 00:03:56.641
Your progress can be saved as a
private draft while you complete the

78
00:03:56.687 --> 00:03:57.186
form.

79
00:03:57.778 --> 00:04:01.540
If the evaluation requires a
signature, use the available signing

80
00:04:01.598 --> 00:04:04.083
options and follow the confirmation
process.

81
00:04:04.582 --> 00:04:06.811
This is a separate PDF-mode session.

82
00:04:07.241 --> 00:04:10.225
It does not switch the structured
session to another evaluation

83
00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:10.886
method.

84
00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:15.171
Before submitting, preview the
completed PDF to verify that your

85
00:04:15.229 --> 00:04:17.493
entries and signature are correctly
positioned.

86
00:04:18.085 --> 00:04:21.486
If you make changes after signing, the
signature must be confirmed

87
00:04:21.521 --> 00:04:22.009
again.

88
00:04:22.438 --> 00:04:26.014
Once the document is accurate and
complete, confirm your review and

89
00:04:26.072 --> 00:04:27.755
submit the final evaluation.

90
00:04:28.255 --> 00:04:31.424
The completed PDF is then locked and
can be downloaded for your

91
00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:31.981
records.

92
00:04:32.573 --> 00:04:35.012
Confirm the current preview after the
final edit.

93
00:04:35.604 --> 00:04:38.750
Submission locks your assessment,
while the coordinator retains

94
00:04:38.808 --> 00:04:41.049
responsibility for the official
result.

95
00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:45.254
After submission, you can revisit your
completed evaluation through

96
00:04:45.289 --> 00:04:48.227
Results or the available defense
evaluation record.

97
00:04:48.819 --> 00:04:52.360
The final document remains available
for review, allowing you to

98
00:04:52.406 --> 00:04:55.599
confirm what was submitted without
changing the locked assessment.

99
00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:57.840
Your account shows its own assessment.

100
00:04:58.432 --> 00:05:01.822
Another panelist's private draft is
outside this demonstration.

101
00:05:02.433 --> 00:05:06.253
Your evaluation contributes to the
defense review process, but your

102
00:05:06.288 --> 00:05:09.086
recommendation does not automatically
determine the official

103
00:05:09.144 --> 00:05:09.712
outcome.

104
00:05:10.305 --> 00:05:13.602
After the required panelist
evaluations are submitted, the

105
00:05:13.671 --> 00:05:16.864
authorized coordinator reviews the
consolidated information and

106
00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.571
releases the official decision.

107
00:05:19.256 --> 00:05:22.275
You can then check the outcome
information made available to you in

108
00:05:22.309 --> 00:05:22.936
the system.

109
00:05:23.528 --> 00:05:26.861
This separate prepared completed
session has already passed those

110
00:05:26.907 --> 00:05:27.720
release checks.

111
00:05:28.149 --> 00:05:31.783
A panelist recommendation alone does
not publish this decision.

112
00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.837
The Panelist workspace also includes
supporting tools for managing

113
00:05:35.918 --> 00:05:37.148
academic activities.

114
00:05:37.578 --> 00:05:40.214
Calendar helps you keep track of
scheduled sessions.

115
00:05:40.806 --> 00:05:44.242
Manuscript Reviews and Official Copies
provide access to the

116
00:05:44.312 --> 00:05:46.866
research documents available under
your permissions.

117
00:05:47.551 --> 00:05:50.837
Messages and Inbox support
communication and correspondence

118
00:05:50.895 --> 00:05:52.219
related to your assignments.

119
00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:56.038
An empty Official Copies list means no
permitted published copy is

120
00:05:56.085 --> 00:05:56.735
available;

121
00:05:57.165 --> 00:06:00.775
a private draft does not become an
official copy automatically.

122
00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.279
That concludes the ADVISIO Panelist
walkthrough.

123
00:06:04.779 --> 00:06:07.797
You can return to your workspace
anytime to prepare for upcoming

124
00:06:07.832 --> 00:06:11.199
defenses and review your assigned
academic activities.
